					Th.
					8.96
				</span></i>
			 : impers., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρίσταταί μοι</span>
			<i>it occurs</i> to me ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῷ οὐ
				παραστήσεται . . τεθνάναι βούλεσθαι</span> to whom <i>it
				will</i> not <i>occur</i> to wish for death, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				7.46
			</span></i>: folld. by <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡς</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				4.61
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				95
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				12.62
			</span></i>, etc. : c. inf., <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				7.17
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐχὶ παρίσταταί μοι ταὐτὰ γιγνώσκειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					3.1
				</span></i>
			 : c. acc. et inf., <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				21.12
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phd.</u>
				58e
			</span></i>; part., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ παριστάμενον</span>
			<i>that which comes into one's head, a thought</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Cont.</u>
				13
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ τοῦ π. λέγειν</span> speak
